@slackwater/database

This package holds code and data under different licenses.

The code is licensed under the MIT License. See LICENSE for the license and
its copyright holders.

The station data is licensed per station, not by LICENSE as a whole. Each
station carries its license in its `license` field: public domain, CC BY 4.0,
Japan's Government Standard Terms of Use 2.0 or CC BY-NC 4.0 from its source,
or MIT, the license this project gives its own registry records and the
Canadian Hydrographic Service station identities. Stations under CC BY-NC 4.0 are
marked `commercial_use: false`. The readers return them like any other station,
so a commercial use has to filter them out. Each station's `attribution` field
holds the credit its source requires; display it wherever the station's data is
shown. The release's .tcd file has no such fields: each station names its
license in its `restriction` field, "CC BY-NC 4.0" for the non-commercial
ones, and carries any credit it needs in its notes.

The location fields and `context` are derived from GeoNames, the OpenStreetMap
water bodies and Marine Regions, credited below. Pass those credits on wherever
the data is shown, for example in an app's credits screen.

This repository uses GeoNames cities500 data under CC BY 4.0 to derive station
location fields. This product includes data created by GeoNames
(www.geonames.org), licensed under CC BY 4.0:
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

metadata/coastline.geojson is a clipped extract of OpenStreetMap land polygons,
licensed under ODbL 1.0. Credit: OpenStreetMap contributors.
https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/

Station context names the OpenStreetMap bay or strait a station sits in,
derived from metadata/water-bodies.geojson, an extract of OpenStreetMap
licensed under ODbL 1.0. Credit: OpenStreetMap contributors.
https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/

Station countries for registry records are derived from
metadata/maritime-zones.geojson, an extract of the Marine Regions Maritime
Boundaries Geodatabase (Exclusive Economic Zones) by the Flanders Marine
Institute (marineregions.org), licensed under CC BY 4.0:
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

Country names and continent metadata derive from the pinned c5y-n8r binary,
using Wikidata structured data under CC0 1.0:
https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Wikidata:Licensing
The distribution includes countries.crdb, country-evidence.json and
country-release.json under dist/generated/, with the upstream data terms
and MIT code license in COUNTRY_DATA_LICENSE.md and C5Y_N8R_LICENSE.
